              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Write each all-nines term as a power of ten minus one; the result has 318 ones followed by 0789.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Each term with $k$ digits is $10^k-1$. There are 321 terms.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=(10-1)+(100-1)+\\cdots+(10^{321}-1)\\\\N&=(10+100+\\cdots+10^{321})-321\\\\N&=\\underbrace{111\\cdots111}_{321\\text{ ones}}0-321\\\\N&=\\underbrace{111\\cdots111}_{318\\text{ ones}}0789\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe sum of the digits is $318\\times1+0+7+8+9=342$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
